hello and welcome to Playstation grenade  box night battle royale players  continually improve with every single  game the days of easy wins are numbered  and to be able to compete for victories  proves harder every day with that in  mind I wanted to bring you eight console  settings and secrets which I believe  will improve your game so if you're one  of those people who can only play on the  weekend this should help you stand  shoulder to shoulder with those that put  in 40 hours a week you ready let's do  this let's start with the most obvious  but also the most frightening to anyone  who has been playing from the start  the combat pro controller setting I'll  say it simply you must change to this  setup as quickly as you can  most of what I'm going to go through on  this video depends on that setting and I  don't want to waste your time anyway  with combat pro not only can your  weapons be switched to back and forth  but that's also the case for building  options other noticeable improvements  include using r3 to crouch which we all  know improves accuracy the old system  forced us to stop aiming to perform the  Crouch animation but was this way your  right thumb is always on the stick and  there's no excuse not to crouch before  firing I know it seems daunting to  switch control options especially if  you're hitting your mid twenties and  your ability to unlearn is quite a  struggle but stick with it I promise in  the long run you'll pick up more  victories I didn't win for 20 games  whilst learning combat pro and  considered switching back so many times  I feel your pain now that's out of the  way we can get to the real meat of this  video and a huge tip I want to offer how  often do you use the pyramid structure I  personally only use it to trap enemies  which isn't vital here's my suggestion  during the game lobby use the Edit  function to remove two of the furthest  squares away thus creating a ramp I know  it sounds ridiculous but let me explain  the input lag in game can be horrendous  the more button presses in a short  period of time increases this issue and  causes this stuttering effect in battle  we want to eliminate as much lag and  desynchronisation as possible and that's  why I use the pyramid  Niq let's put it into action let's build  a wall under ramp twice in standard  settings it takes 11 button prompts in  combat pro it takes well it still takes  11 button presses so that's not the best  way to showcase the combat pro option  but if we switch to the pyramid ramp  configuration we can knock off three  inputs from 11 button presses down to 8  what more in this quick scenario the  pyramid ramp build was 2 seconds faster  than the other options 2 seconds in  battle is a lifetime so I hope you  consider this option and if you're still  not convinced keep in mind the lag  issues less button presses usually mean  less chance of stutter lag which  infuriates us all in addition to this as  we aren't using the original ramp it can  be edited into something else for  example I like to rotate the ramp to a  down slope for safe descending from  roofs  I'm currently testing out the spiral  staircase option to allow me to build  vertically if stuck next to a mountain  simply puts by utilizing the pyramid you  can customize your build options  pre-fight to complement your play style  I really hope you consider it let's talk  about aiming on console and more  importantly aim-assist aim-assist is  most definitely needed on console as  your thumbs cannot gain the accuracy  compared to a keyboard and mouse if  you're playing on a pad don't turn it  off when aim assist works with you it  feels great and the random spread  element keeps us on our toes in the  search results headshots but the issues  arise when a misis works against you  have you ever been in a scenario where  you seem to be stuck behind the target  unable to hit them it's bloody stressful  isn't it well don't worry too much it  isn't a reflection of your ability it's  simply an aim assist issue we can't  solve but we can combat let's quickly  make sure we know what aim assist is as  your reticle crosses the target or  rather the vicinity of the target the  aim assist kicks in and helps stabilize  your shots towards the target in recent  updates this has been reduced massively  and thankfully the snipers no longer use  it but it doesn't do the job for you it  only assists the motions of your thumbs  if you begin to fire behind an opponent  the aim assist kicks in and actively  prevent you from  catching up to your target to stop this  we have two options the first is to move  your thumbs past the target but you will  need to exert additional pressure to  make it work  alternately you must stop firing  reacquire your targets and once again  start shooting essentially we all need  to lead our targets and allow them to  run into the bullets by doing this the  aim assist will live up to its name and  desist your accuracy we can go a step  further than this with our next point  it's time to talk about sensitivity  settings and right away I want to state  categorically that sensitivity is  completely subjective everyone is  different so don't let anyone make this  decision for you try on low medium and  high sensitivities until you find your  zone you'll need to play for hours for  your muscle-memory to adapt and those  tiny bits of fine-tuning that you will  need to make let's break down the pros  and cons so you can make an educated  decision low sensitivity is all about  bigger movements with your thumbs if  you're quite heavy-handed or if you play  in a freezing cold room this should be  your starting point when choosing  sensitivity when it comes to ranged  accuracy low sensitivity rules the roost  and by love sensitivity I mean between  one and three in your settings fights  from long and medium distances are  dominated by low sensitivity players so  if you prefer to use the assault rifle  burst rifle and to a lesser extent the  snipers think about trying controller  sensitivity 3 it's far easier to track a  target at range with a sensitivity  around 3 and there's a kicker to this to  the aim assist is hugely improved making  ranged encounters of breeze so put  bluntly low sensitivity will help the  aim assist high sensitivity on the other  hand will make range encounters a little  harder at first not impossible though  with practice a high sense player can  wipe the floor with anyone at distance  but as a starting point there is that  small issue of aim assist working  against you but we've already looked at  that the benefits for high sensitivity  around 6 and upwards allows for tiny  movements in your thumb sticks to be  recognized as official inputs this gives  players a huge range of motion compared  to  place Hisense is ideal for up close and  personal combats  so you double-pumped players you should  consider a higher setting to allow for  mobility when jumping around like a  headless chicken I was hoping to use my  own footage here but I hate double-pump  probably because I'm terrible at it high  sensitivity is great for verticality and  as we all know for tonight is all about  the high ground Anakin another little  advantage to high sensitivity is the  ability to look behind your character  without losing any speed watch any  professional player and you'll notice  the jump spin they constantly do to  check behind them on console this is  only possible with a sensitivity around  7 and above by using this you can run  into battle and check your flanks  without losing any momentum at all Oh  before I forget if your part is getting  a little old and worn out and you play  on a high sensitivity you may find  yourself doing this because of wear and  tear the thumbstick slightly pushes to  the side only a micro amount but if  you're on a high sensitive setting then  the game thinks that you want to run in  circles so you'll be stuck like this  you'll either need to buy a new pad or  lower the sensitivity to prolong the  life of your current pad on low  sensitivity the tiny offsets of your  thumbsticks would be completely ignored  by the console there's so much more  detail we could go into about controller  sensitivity but at this point I just  wanted to get the basics into all  console players at present I play in the  middle of both sensitivities after I  took a fortnight off bought night  there's a joke in there somewhere I came  back and found my settings were too high  and I reverted back to these starting at  6 I will play a handful of matches and  slowly change my sensitivity back up to  8 because I'm trying to get better with  shotguns I'm adapting my game due to the  horrific double-pumped meta which I do  hate but I need to stay competitive keep  in mind all this comes down to muscle  memory which can take many hours to  change so make a decision and slowly get  used to it but don't be afraid to adapt  to fine-tune to match your skillset and  always remember aiming down sights or AD  s and scope settings can be trained  independently of general sensitivity  that was far more in-depth than I  planned so let's go through a few  settings you may want to consider back  in the ps2 days aim and fire were always  on l1 and r1 rather than the triggers  underneath this was switched when the  trigger buttons were redesigned to feel  the same as gun triggers but they  actually take a fraction more time to  press and release than if you were using  l1 and r1 it's possible to switch these  buttons if you see fit on ps4 find  settings and accessibility and turn on  button assignments from here you can  reassign anything you desire while we're  here those of you who jump a great deal  in battle should consider switching the  assigned jump button to either a  shoulder button or a thumb trigger the  theory is simple to jump in the original  settings you must take your thumb away  from aiming for a split second unless  you hold the pad like a claw of course  switching the button here will result in  both your thumbs staying on the  thumbsticks and therefore more headshots  I've got to admit I wasn't going to  include that point as I hate double  pumper so much but it's for the greater  good I suppose whilst we're in the  settings let's improve our quality of  life with a few changes here if you are  ever searching a chest and your thumb  slips off the button and change the tap  to search function and now only a single  press is required in here I also make  sure I turn off vibration for a few  reasons  I find it impairs me for a split second  and also I like to preserve the battery  life and if you're on ps4 you will know  about the battery issues  I also recommend turning on the reset  building option which will always make a  wall the first option in your  construction arsenal if you are great at  remembering what the last thing you did  then switch this off but if you put down  random floors mid-battle yeah keep it on  to minimize issues  one more thing while we're here I also  recommend switching the option to stop  reloads when sprinting being stuck in a  load animation will lead to your death  from time to time but by using this  option you can safely run away before  you die pumping  into a shotgun this one is an old one  but the addition of the Black Knight I  think it needs revisiting brightness if  you have any trouble locating dark  characters under trees or in bushes and  crank this setting up I've had a great  deal of success sitting under the trees  when playing as the Black Knight not  many people tend to check trees but with  that skin on it's a real struggle to  spot so I'll stay ahead of the curve and  smash the brightness through the roof  only issue it looks awful detracts from  the game's beauty another stupidly  obvious one to end on but I think it  needs to be said again if you are  playing bar tonight put on a pair of  headphones to hear everything if you're  playing on your living room TV you'll be  surprised how many footsteps distant  sounds you were just completely missing  do yourself a favor and grab a headset  to even up the battlefield so there we  have it eight console settings and  secrets which I believe will improve  your game let me know what you think and  if the pyramid ramp technique is worth a  try  with 60fps coming to consoles soon time  saved using modded ramps will be  invaluable if I've missed anything let  me know and jump on our disco to chat  about fortnight and other video games  I'm Adam from Playstation grenade it's  been a bloody pleasure like always I'll  see you next time  [Music]

